<title>USA: Clinton wants to extend railroad inspection fees.</title>
<headline>Clinton wants to extend railroad inspection fees.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Clinton administration said Thursday it will offer legislation to permanently extend railroad safety inspection fees that were enacted in 1990, but expired at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>In its fiscal 1998 budget plan, the White House said the fee would be expanded to cover hours of service and hazardous materials inspections.</p>
<p>The fee offsets costs incurred by the Federal Railroad Administration for inspection, enforcement and other activities for safe operation of passenger and freight railroads.</p>
</text>
